WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:05.440
Defects in retinal genes cause

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.183
a devastating from of childhood blindness.

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:11.920
Gene therapy is really,
I think at the forefront

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.690
of treating retinal degenerations.

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:17.400
There are now over 20 clinical trials

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.660
addressing various diseases in ways that

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:22.250
we didn't really think possible before.

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:23.083
Come on.

00:00:23.083 --> 00:00:26.270
Having to make a decision
on his behalf has been

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:27.790
a real struggle.

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:31.000
This treatment could change our lives,

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.723
this could stop a truly terrible disease.

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:38.700
As we tackle the problem of

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:42.020
childhood blindness, this is
going to be a real breakthrough

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:44.660
in our ability to change
the course of the disease

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:46.410
in a way we never thought possible.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:01.200
Maverick is my firstborn
child, he has been

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.610
the most amazing child to raise

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:05.690
from the day that he was born.

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:07.950
I didn't have a lot of
experience with babies

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:10.320
before I had him, but I just noticed

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:13.010
that he had a blank stare.

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:18.010
Checked his tracking vision
and it was non-existent.

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:20.940
We went through all the genetic testing

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:25.770
and it came back positive for
Leber's congenital amaurosis

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:28.673
with a specific genetic marker of RPE65.

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:37.060
The cones and the rods in
the eyes don't allow for

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:40.980
light perception so he is legally blind

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:44.683
with specifically low-light blindness.

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:48.530
He also doesn't have peripheral vision

00:01:48.530 --> 00:01:50.510
or vision below his waste.

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.140
It's almost tunnel vision.

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:55.573
Ahh, I need a parachute now, help me!

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:01.593
Up here is my room,

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:05.650
and these are my pillows.

00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:07.083
This is my eye patch.

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:11.200
It has to be the right
lighting for him to see.

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:16.200
Once the sun goes down,
his world is very dark.

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:18.930
We take him inside, turn on all the lights

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:20.313
until it's time for bed.

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:28.863
Maverick's condition is degenerative.

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:36.830
There is no timeframe
of when the degeneration

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:41.470
will take place, but
it is a well-known fact

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:45.330
that he will be completely
blind in later years.

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:48.210
It took his thoughts
quite some time to subside

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:53.210
into sense of fire and
sulfur, a torched landscape.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:58.940
In December of 2017, the
FDA approved gene therapy

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:03.510
for Maverick's specific
condition and so we went

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:06.713
and talked to Dr. Nagiel
shortly after it was approved.

00:03:08.613 --> 00:03:10.360
Oh, mine goes right behind you.

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:12.910
Maverick was six years
old when I first met him,

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:16.320
and this family, for a
long time had struggled

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:19.480
with getting a diagnosis,
and then we're very excited

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:21.630
finally to hear that
there was a treatment.

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:25.310
Luxturna is a gene replacement therapy

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:28.050
whereby we're delivering
a normal health copy

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:33.050
of the RPE65 gene to patients
who have two defective copies.

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:37.220
This medication is a virus
which has essentially

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:39.680
been modified so its only job

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:42.433
is to deliver the genetic material.

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:46.490
We deliver this virus
with a very fine needle

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:50.080
underneath the retina and
then we have a healthy copy

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:51.560
of a gene that's been missing

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:53.483
in the cells that normally make it.

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:56.840
Unfortunately with this disease,

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:59.830
the cells that absorb the
light, the photo receptors,

00:03:59.830 --> 00:04:02.520
are constantly degenerating
and there gets to be a point

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:05.400
where there simply aren't
enough cells to function

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:07.683
even if we were to deliver that gene back.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.820
So it makes a lot of sense to treat

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:15.560
earlier pediatric patients,
young patients when they

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:18.270
have those cells there and
just need the normal copy

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:21.030
of the gene to make the
protein functioning again.

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:24.410
So treatment early in children
is really the way to go

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:26.240
to achieve the best results.

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:28.160
Here at Children's Hospital Los Angeles,

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:31.720
we've treated 17 patients, so 34 eyes.

00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:34.400
We have data that the
treatment effect is stable

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:36.580
without any loss in function.

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:40.120
Five years ago, there were no
treatments for this disease

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:44.160
and for the bulk of retinal
generations, these patients,

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:46.060
if they were lucky, they got a diagnosis

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:49.350
with genetic testing but
beyond that, there wasn't much

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:51.110
that we could do aside from

00:04:51.110 --> 00:04:53.640
get the most out of the
vision that they have.

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:56.540
Since the FDA approval of
Luxturna, that's really opened

00:04:56.540 --> 00:05:00.900
the door to not just
treating this relatively rare

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.040
retinal degeneration, but essentially

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:04.413
any retinal degeneration.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:10.970
This has been probably the
most difficult decision

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:14.320
that I've ever had to
make in my entire life.

00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:17.440
It makes me very nervous
because it is so new,

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:19.580
if it doesn't go well, it's my fault

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:22.403
because I chose to do this to my child.

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:25.610
I honestly feel like I hit the jackpot

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:26.950
when I had Maverick.

00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:29.960
I don't know any other seven-year-old kid

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:33.290
that could handle everything
that he has been through

00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:35.940
with such appreciation for life, you know?

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:39.703
He is willing to do or try anything.

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:43.630
All right, here we go.

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:47.653
After today, our life could
potentially change forever.

00:05:54.406 --> 00:05:56.906
I love you.
I love you, buddy.

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:01.700
He might go back home
and for the first time

00:06:01.700 --> 00:06:04.500
have fun with his friends by
the pool as it's getting dark,

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:06.920
ride his bike at dusk,
go trick-or-treating,

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:09.070
these are the sort of
improvements that really

00:06:09.070 --> 00:06:11.700
change a child's life
and the motor confidence

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:14.670
that comes with ambulating and interacting

00:06:14.670 --> 00:06:16.830
with the environment in a way
that they couldn't before,

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:19.387
I think really has life-long consequences.

00:06:59.630 --> 00:07:02.120
It takes seven days for the corrected DNA

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:05.990
to be absorbed so at seven days,

00:07:05.990 --> 00:07:08.833
he could potentially see again.

00:07:13.090 --> 00:07:18.090
It just comes in very small
doses and it could take

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:20.070
up to four months, they said.

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:37.430
Maverick had his two
surgeries, and we are home.

00:07:38.530 --> 00:07:40.820
The first day that I really noticed

00:07:40.820 --> 00:07:43.420
that something was different
was riding in the car,

00:07:43.420 --> 00:07:46.730
and he said mom, I'm just looking outside

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:49.497
and I'm seeing what is outside the window,

00:07:49.497 --> 00:07:51.930
like I've never been able
to see through the windows

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:55.010
and it seemed so small but
it was really life changing

00:07:55.010 --> 00:07:58.213
for him to be able to
look out of a window.

00:07:59.270 --> 00:08:03.040
Okay, listen to me.
One more game of tag.

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:04.800
Maverick, sit.
Ready?

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:05.790
One more game.

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:10.205
One, two, three, four,
five, I'm coming out!

00:08:10.205 --> 00:08:13.751
I see you guys!

00:08:19.690 --> 00:08:21.760
In the past seven years,
we don't even come

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:22.980
in the backyard at night.

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:25.103
This is a true miracle.

00:08:26.255 --> 00:08:28.588
You can not stop me!

00:08:30.521 --> 00:08:32.383
Okay, I've got Maverick.

00:08:32.383 --> 00:08:35.113
Willow, come here, get him.

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:40.700
He has a whole new level of independence

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:44.607
and he is ready to conquer
anything that is given to him.

